### How do I calculate my monthly loan repayment based on the loan amount I need to buy a property?\n\nPlan your monthly expenses with our Home Loan Calculator.\n\n##### I'm planning to buy a new house for the first time. What should I do?\n\nHere are simple steps on how to buy a new house in Malaysia.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWestside 3, Desa ParkCity Review | PropertyGuru Malaysia (https://www.propertyguru.com.my/new-property-launch/reviews/westside-3-desa-parkcity-215601)\nciteturn241search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.4 years ago; Crawled: today; They were also previously contracted by Perdana ParkCity for the construction of One Central Park, a 45-storey condominium, which was delivered over three months ahead of schedule in October 2016. ... A 1,099 sq ft Westside 3 unit listed for sale on PropertyGuru in April 2021 is about RM1.05 million.\n\n# Westside 3, Desa ParkCity\n\n  * Review\n\n  * Caitlyn\n  * ⋅\n  * 4 May 2021\n\nWestside 3, also referred to as Westside III, is located at the highly successful 473-acre Desa ParkCity. The RM505 million condominium project is developed by Perdana ParkCity Sdn Bhd, the property arm of Samling Group.\n\nWestside III condominium is developed over 4.27 acres of freehold land, and it achieved a 59% take-up rate (276 units of the 469 units) after its priority launch event on 30 May 2015. The developer mentioned that the interest shown is indeed remarkable given the market sentiment then. There were more than 100 people queueing in front of the sales gallery at 6:30am. Some buyers camped there since 26 May. The award-winning master-planned township of Desa ParkCity has a track record of attracting strong sales for all its launches.\n\nWestside III condominium was constructed by GDB Holdings Bhd, and they completed the project ahead of its contractual completion date. They were also previously contracted by Perdana ParkCity for the construction of One Central Park, a 45-storey condominium, which was delivered over three months ahead of schedule in October 2016.\n\nAddress: Jalan Residen Utama, Desa Parkcity, 52200 Kuala Lumpur\n\nDeveloper: Perdana ParkCity Sdn Bhd\n\nProperty Type: Condominium\n\nLand Area: 4.27 acres\n\nLand Title: Residential\n\nTenure: Freehold\n\nNo. of Blocks: 1\n\nNo. of Storeys: 47\n\nTotal Units: 469\n\nYear of Completion: 2019\n\nBuilt-up Area: 1,077 sq ft – 1,927 sq ft\n\nFacilities:\n\nStreet Level\n\n  * Guardhouse\n  * Jogging track\n  * Sun deck\n  * Water amusement park with water jet\n  * Secret garden\n  * Sunrise garden\n  * Pavilion\n  * Forest\n  * Adventure playground\n  * Tennis court\n  * Parlor\n\nFacility deck (Level 6)\n\n  * Facility deck link bridge\n  * Facility deck lift lobby\n  * Gym\n  * Activity deck\n  * Leisure pool / 40m lap pool\n  * Jet pool / shallow pool\n  * Spa pool\n  * Jacuzzi pool\n  * Multi-purpose hall\n  * Terrace\n  * Barbeque area\n  * Kids’ funzone with play apparatus\n\nSky garden\n\n  * Level 3, 6, 10, 13a, 18, 22, 26, 30, 33a, 38, 42 & 46\n\nLaunch Price: From RM684,972\n\nLaunch Price Per Sq Ft: From RM636 per sq ft\n\nMaintenance Fee: RM0.36 per sq ft\n\n### Project Details\n\nThe units at Westside 3 have a built-up area of between 1,077 sq ft and 1,927 sq ft. The partly furnished units come in 6 types (Type A1, Type A2, Type A3, Type B1, Type C1, and Type C2), and 3 layouts (2 bedrooms + 2 bathrooms, 3 bedrooms + 2 bathrooms, and 3 bedrooms + 4 bathrooms).\n\nThe single-phase 47-storey project has a total of 469 units, and the prices started from RM636 per sq ft. The maintenance fee is 36 sen per sq ft. Facilities are on the Street Level and Level 6. They include gardens, sun decks, water amusement park with water jet, adventure playground, tennis court, jogging track, pools, barbeque area, kids’ funzone, and multi-purpose hall, among others. These facilities are exclusively for Westside 3 residents and their guests.\n\nEach unit come with high-quality interiors, with air-conditioners. Each bathroom also come with hot water supply and shower screens. An intercom is also available in each unit, for added security. There are also 1,079 parking bays for residents across 5 levels. The project was completed in 2019, and majority of the buyers were owner-occupiers.\n\nThe developer has kept the design concept for its condominiums, which is to create a neighbourhood that encourages interaction amongst neighours. Apart from interaction at the public facilities, the developer has included water dispensers at the lobby, as a point where neighbours could have a chat. They have applied this same concept for Westside 1 and Westside 2.\n\nUnit Types  | Built-Up\nType A1  | ·         1,077 sq ft / 1,099 sq ft / 1,163 sq ft / 1,196 sq ft ·         2 bedrooms ·         2 bathrooms\nType A2  | ·         1,228 sq ft / 1,250 sq ft / 1,336 sq ft ·         2 bedrooms ·         2 bathrooms\nType A3  | ·         1,271 sq ft / 1,281 sq ft / 1,377 sq ft ·         2 bedrooms ·         2 bathrooms\nType B1  | ·         1,443 sq ft / 1,454 sq ft / 1,561 sq ft / 1,583 sq ft ·         3 bedrooms ·         2 bathrooms\nType C1  | ·         1,529 sq ft / 1,540 sq ft / 1,680 sq ft ·         3 bedrooms ·         4 bathrooms\nType C2  | ·         1,788 sf / 1,798sf / 1,927sf ·         3 bedrooms + Study + Utility ·         4 bathrooms\n\n\n  * The International School @ ParkCity\n  * SMK Desa Mahkota\n  * SJK (C) Kepong (3) ParkCity\n  * Menjalara High School\n  * Sekolah Menengah Kebangsaan Sinar Bintang\n  * SK Bandar Sri Damansara 3\n\nMedical Care\n\n  * ParkCity Medical Centre\n\nShopping\n\n  * The Waterfront\n  * Plaza Arkadia\n  * ParkCity TownCenter\n  * Lotus’s Kepong\n  * Kepong Village Mall\n  * Damansara Avenue\n  * Decathlon Sri Damansara\n  * 1 Utama\n  * The Curve\n  * IPC Shopping Centre\n\nRecreation\n\n  * The Central Park\n  * Sunway SPK Damansara Basketball Court\n  * Bukit Sri Bintang Peak\n  * Taman Tasik Menjalara\n\n### Analysis\n\nWestside 3 was targeted at families, first-time homebuyers, and upgraders. The developer also noted that an increasing number of families have not been hiring maids due to cost and availability. Therefore, the developer started their own premium maid service, ParkCity Cleaners. The service is available to all residents in Desa ParkCity.\n\nDespite the slowdown in the property market, values and rents in Desa ParkCity have remained resilient. There are several factors that lend to this, including a growing expatriate community, the medical centre and international school, daily conveniences, security, and various amenities available to residents.\n\nThe Northshore Gardens at Desa ParkCity was launched in 2008 and priced at RM650 per sq ft for the smaller units. A search in PropertyGuru in April 2021, shows that they are going for about RM950 per sq ft. As for Westside 3, it was launched from RM636 per sq ft in 2015, and listings show that units range from RM850 per sq ft to slightly above RM1,000 per sq ft. These prices are way above those in the neighbouring Kepong area, and matching those in Mont’Kiara.\n\nA 1,099 sq ft Westside 3 unit listed for sale on PropertyGuru in April 2021 is about RM1.05 million. For monthly rent, it is listed at approximately RM3,400. Thus, the gross rental yield for such a unit would roughly be 3.89% per annum.\n\nHere’s a quick look at residential properties in the area.\n\nProject  | Land Tenure  | Property Type  | Completion  | Built-up  | Approximate Launch Price\nWestside 3 by Perdana ParkCity Sdn Bhd  | Freehold  | Condominium  | 2019  | 1,077 sq ft – 1,927 sq ft  | From RM684,972\nMenjalara 18 Residences by Radiant Symphony Sdn Bhd  | Freehold  | Condominium  | 2009  | 1,316 sq ft – 3,120 sq ft  | From RM190 per sq ft\nSunway SPK 3 Harmoni by Sunway City Bhd & SPK Bhd  | Freehold  | Townhouse  | 2015  | 2,336 sq ft – 2,583 sq ft  | From RM857,000\nDamansara Foresta by Land & General Berhad  | Freehold  | Condominium  | 2015  | 1,425 sq ft – 1,610 sq ft  | From RM570,000 (Block A)\nAtivo Suites at Damansara Avenue by TA Global Berhad  | Freehold  | Serviced Residence  | 2021  | 499 sq ft – 1,498 sq ft  | From RM481,000\nVIM 3 by VST Development Sdn Bhd  | Leasehold  | Serviced Apartment  | 2020  | 460 sq ft – 920 sq ft  | From RM289,800\nMizumi Residences by Wawasan Metro Bina Sdn Bhd  | Leasehold  | Condominium  | 2020  | 901 sq ft – 1,027 sq ft  | From RM388,000\nEast Parc @ Menjalara by Fiamma Holdings Bhd  | Leasehold  | Serviced Apartment  | 2020  | 600 sq ft – 1,522 sq ft  | From RM424,900\n\nShow More\n\n### Summary\n\nOnce the market picks up, well-planned townships could rebound first, and at a faster pace. Ultimately, what usually makes a township successful is a focus on residents. Desa ParkCity is a thriving township, and some see it as a good place to get away from the city without being too far away from Kuala Lumpur. There are schools, clinics, shops, eateries, and recreational facilities, all within its township.\n\nAccording to a public online forum, Westside 3 is close to the NKVE. So, that could mean some noise and dust pollution. It would be best to decide it for yourself. Westside 3 is slightly further from the facilities in the township, and that also means that it is further from the crowds, and thus, could mean a quieter environment.\n\nIf you’re interested in a 1,099 sq ft unit at Westside 3 that’s priced at RM1.05 million, here are its estimated loan figures.\n\n  * LTV / margin of finance: 80%\n  * Down payment (20%): RM210,000\n  * Loan amount: RM840,000\n  * Loan term: 30 years\n  * Interest rate: 3.2%\n  * Monthly repayment: RM3,772\n  * Approximate required gross annual income: RM146,000*\n\nCalculations are based on the PropertyGuru Home Loan Calculator, and PropertyGuru Home Loan Eligibility and Affordability Calculator. Try them to estimate the figures that are right for you!\n\nIf you’re interested in calculating Debt Service Ratio (DSR), you may ref